# GitHub Workflow

Git commits/branches: `git-workflow-and-versioning`. Issues/PRs/labels/assignees: this rule.

When creating or editing GitHub issues or PRs, load `.cursor/skills/github-workflow/SKILL.md`. Do not improvise `gh` flags.

## Discover, don't invent

Before any GitHub write:

```bash
gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,defaultBranchRef
gh label list
gh api "repos/$(gh repo view --json nameWithOwner -q .nameWithOwner)/collaborators" --jq '.[].login'
```

Never create labels. Never assign or request-review a login that is not in that collaborators list. Never request review from the PR author.

## Before opening a PR

- **Non-trivial** (multi-file, behavior/API/CI change, new rule/skill, anything that needs discussion): an issue must exist or be created. PR body must contain `Closes #N`.
- **One-file chore** with no behavior change: issue optional. Do not invent `Closes`.
- **Automated sync PRs**: add `automated` if that label exists. No issue required.

## Labels

Exactly one type label, and only if it exists in `gh label list`:

- `bug` — broken behavior
- `enhancement` — new capability
- `chore` — maintenance, config, deps
- `documentation` — docs-only

Add `automated` only on bot/sync PRs, in addition to the type. If the needed type is missing, ask. Do not apply triage labels (`wontfix`, `duplicate`, `invalid`, `question`, `good first issue`, `help wanted`) on new work.

## Assign and review

- Assignee: `--assignee "@me"` when the authenticated user is a collaborator. If other humans have push, ask who owns it.
- Reviewer: request only other collaborators (or CODEOWNERS). Solo repo: `gh pr review --comment` — never `--approve` your own PR.
- Merge only after `gh pr checks` is green.
